// Assigning to a WHOLE fixed array (not an element) is unsupported. Every spelling was
// already broken: a non-literal RHS reached an invalid ptr -> [N x T] bitcast and failed
// module verification, while a string literal folded that cast into a ConstantExpr the
// verifier does not check - which miscompiled to garbage, or crashed the compiler in
// SelectionDAG on an indexed read. Element assignment (`b[i] = ...`) is unaffected.
expect_error("assignment to a whole fixed array 'int[3]' is not supported") {
    void f() { int[3] a = default; int[3] b = default; b = a; }
}

// A union's ARRAY ARM is still a whole fixed array, so the whole-array reject covers it.
// The remedy must name the receiver AS WRITTEN ('u.a'), not the base variable 'u' - an
// element write into a union array field is legal and is a value leg in test_basic.cb.
union WholeArmUnion { int[3] a; char[12] b; };
expect_error("assign its elements ('u.a[i] = ...')") {
    void g() { WholeArmUnion u = default; WholeArmUnion v = default; u.a = v.a; }
}
